From d1dabff09bd7505b11b4be845b9dce772ee3dbe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cdeletre <cyril.deletre@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:41:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] native: twin stick controls from the input bits 22-31, where
 a match allows them

The console (port/native/platform/input_sdl.cpp) puts a code in the input
bits the original never uses: 0 classic controls, 1 twin stick, 2 + angle / 3
twin stick aiming. It travels with the keys, so every machine decodes the same
thing; it is read only alone or in a match whose players all said they know it
(gGta2PortTwinAllowed, from the lobby's match). With a code the direction keys
walk the ped north, south, west and east on screen, the ped turns toward the
aim (or where it walks, 24 degrees a tick), walks sideways or backwards as it
faces (Char_B4::Update_545720: the step and the velocity go the walking way),
and fires where it faces without the lock-on (Ped::ComputeAimAngle_45C9D0);
a fire truck's, tank's or gun jeep's roof gun turns toward the aim
(Car_BC::RotateRoofObjectTowardTarget_440C10). Driving is unchanged. The
browser is unchanged too: it never plays in a match that allows the bits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
